        "textEn": "Temple of Horus at Edfu\n\nDedicated to Horus, the falcon-headed god, Edfu Temple is the best-preserved temple in Egypt. Built during the Ptolemaic period, its towering pylons, grand courtyard, and detailed inscriptions provide remarkable insight into ancient Egyptian religion.\n\nGebel El Silsila\n\nThis narrow sandstone gorge served as Egypt's primary quarry during the New Kingdom. Stone from these quarries was used to build many of Egypt's great temples. Visitors can explore rock-cut shrines, stelae, and ancient inscriptions left by pharaohs and workers.\n\nSunset Dinner on the Nile\n\nOne of the highlights of a Dahabiya journey is dining under the stars on a secluded Nile island, surrounded by the peaceful sounds of nature.\n\nOvernight at Gebel El Silsila."
